ty provider issue or token/session validation problem rather than a single host failure. Resource usage is elevated but not clearly saturated.\",\"recommended_actions\":[\"Check identity_provider health, error rate, latency, and recent config/certificate/key rotation changes.\",\"Verify auth-api token validation settings, JWKS/cache refresh, clock skew, and issuer/audience configuration.\",\"Compare failure rate by deployment version 2026.06.1, 2026.06.2, and 2026.06.3 to rule out a bad rollout.\",\"Inspect auth-01/auth-02 logs for provider timeout, invalid signature, expired token, or permission-denied patterns.\",\"If customer impact is ongoing, fail over to the secondary identity provider or known-good auth path per runbook.\",\"Invalidate only confirmed bad sessions or tokens after validating blast radius.\"],\"safe_remediation_actions\":[\"SIMULATE: Check identity_provider status and auth-api dependency latency.\",\"SIMULATE: Validate token/JWKS configuration and certificate/key rotation state.\",\"SIMULATE: Compare auth failures by deployment version and host.\",\"SIMULATE: Fail over identity provider using approved runbook after operator approval.\",\"SIMULATE: Invalidate bad sessions only after confirmation.\",\"SIMULATE: Escalate to auth service owner and identity provider owner.\"]}","incident_status":"COMPLETED","investigation_status":"COMPLETED","action":"splunk_webhook_triaged","sourcetype":"aiops-incidents"}
