rn affected both catalog hosts, produced 500/502/503 responses, and showed no dependency failure. DB pool usage was elevated but below saturation, so it is likely a secondary load symptom rather than the root cause.\",\n  \"recommended_actions\": [\n    \"Scale catalog-api capacity or route traffic away from saturated instances.\",\n    \"Inspect catalog-api CPU hotspots for /products requests, including query processing, serial","incident_status":"COMPLETED","investigation_status":"COMPLETED","action":"splunk_webhook_triaged","sourcetype":"aiops-incidents"}
