{"timestamp":"2026-06-13T18:32:28.955+05:30","incident_id":"inc-9210424122","service":"payment-api","status":"COMPLETED","severity":"HIGH","root_cause":"Upstream dependency failure, most likely in the payment_gateway path, with secondary impact from retry-driven latency inflation.","confidence_score":0.84,"evidence_summary":"50 events for payment-api across payment-01 and payment-02. Primary signals were upstream_api_failure and latency_regression. One direct 502 on /payments/capture referenced payment_gateway; other events showed sustained latency up to 1479 ms across /payments/authorize and /payments/capture. Resource metrics were elevated but not saturated (max_cpu_pct 72, max_memory_pct 77.8, max_db_pool_pct 69.09), which makes host exhaustion less likely than dependency degradation.","ai_summary":"The incident is consistent with an upstream dependency outage or brownout rather than a local app failure. Error patterns center on upstream_api_failure with broad latency regression across both hosts and both payment endpoints, while CPU, memory, and DB pool usage remain below critical saturation. The most probable mechanism is dependency instability causing retries and tail-latency spikes.","llm_provider":"codex","mcp_evidence_summary":"MCP client call: MCP evidence for payment-api: 50 events; errors=latency_regression, upstream_api_failure; hosts=payment-01, payment-02; endpoints=/payments/authorize, /payments/capture; dependencies=identity_provider, none, payment_gateway, postgres; avg_latency_ms=453; max_latency_ms=1479; max_cpu_pct=72; max_db_pool_pct=69.","alert_name":"AIOps - Incident Candidate Alert","host":"unknown-host","mcp_investigation":true,"mcp_tools_used":["splunk_run_query"],"spl_queries_used":[],"mcp_log_event_count":50,"llm_raw_response":"{\n  \"root_cause\": \"Upstream dependency failure, most likely in the payment_gateway path, with secondary impact from retry-driven latency inflation.\",\n  \"severity\": \"HIGH\",\n  \"confidence_score\": 0.84,\n  \"evidence_summary\": \"50 events for payment-api across payment-01 and payment-02. Primary signals were upstream_api_failure and latency_regression. One direct 502 on /payments/capture referenced payment_gateway; other events showed sustained latency up to 1479 ms across /payments/authorize and /payments/capture. Resource metrics were elevated but not saturated (max_cpu_pct 72, max_memory_pct 77.8, max_db_pool_pct 69.09), which makes host exhaustion less likely than dependency degradation.\",\n  \"ai_summary\": \"The incident is consistent with an upstream dependency outage or brownout rather than a local app failure. Error patterns center on upstream_api_failure with broad latency regression across both hosts and both payment endpoints, while CPU, memory, and DB pool usage remain below critical saturation. The most probable mechanism is dependency instability causing retries and tail-latency spikes.\",\n  \"recommended_actions\": [\n    \"Fail over or bypass the affected upstream dependency if a secondary route is available.\",\n    \"Open an escalation with the dependency owner/provider and attach the 502/upstream failure evidence.\",\n    \"Throttle or cap retries and tighten timeout budgets to reduce amplification while the dependency is unhealthy.\",\n    \"Validate whether payment_gateway or identity_provider experienced partial outage, degraded latency, or error-rate spikes during the incident window.\"\n  ],\n  \"safe_remediation_actions\": [\n    \"SIMULATE: fail over upstream dependency\",\n    \"SIMULATE: open provider escalation\",\n    \"SIMULATE: throttle retries\",\n    \"SIMULATE: reduce retry concurrency and confirm timeout settings in a staging or canary environment first\"\n  ]\n}\nCodex MCP enhancement failed: [WinError 206] The filename or extension is too long","incident_status":"COMPLETED","investigation_status":"COMPLETED","action":"splunk_webhook_triaged","sourcetype":"aiops-incidents"}
