 driver.\",\n  \"severity\": \"HIGH\",\n  \"confidence_score\": 0.85,\n  \"evidence_summary\": \"50 events for auth-api across auth-01 and auth-02. Dominant errors are auth_failure, with max latency 4068 ms and average latency 706 ms. Affected endpoints are /login, /session, and /token/refresh. identity_provider is the most frequent dependency in failed events. Resource signals show max CPU 80.3%, memory 78.71%, and DB pool 69.12%, indicating load stress but not saturation severe enough to explain the auth failures alone.\",\n  \"ai_summary\": \"Incident points to auth provider or token validation failure as the primary cause. Error pattern is concentrated on authentication flows across both hosts and multiple regions, with elevated latency and moderate CPU pressure. Evidence supports an external identity/auth path issue more than a pure app or database outage.\",\n  \"recommended_actions\": [\n    \"Verify identity_provider health, token validation, and recent config or certificate changes.\",\n    \"Check for auth service logs correlated with 401/403 spikes and refresh-token failures.\",\n    \"Inspect whether a bad deploy or identity-provider dependency regression aligns with the incident window.\",\n    \"Prepare to invalidate affected sessions only if token corruption or auth state inconsistency is confirmed.\",\n    \"Monitor CPU, latency, and error rate until auth traffic returns to baseline.\"\n  ],\n  \"safe_remediation_actions\": [\n    \"SIMULATE: Fail over identity provider\",\n    \"SIMULATE: Invalidate bad sessions\",\n    \"SIMULATE: Escalate auth service\"\n  ]\n}\nCodex MCP enhancement failed: [WinError 206] The filename or extension is too long","incident_status":"COMPLETED","investigation_status":"COMPLETED","action":"splunk_webhook_triaged","sourcetype":"aiops-incidents"}
