{"timestamp":"2026-06-14T08:29:17.460+05:30","incident_id":"inc-b6d4927579","service":"catalog-api","status":"COMPLETED","severity":"MEDIUM","root_cause":"Service latency regression in catalog-api","confidence_score":0.85,"evidence_summary":"50 events for catalog-api show sustained latency regression across catalog-01 and catalog-02. Affected endpoints include /products, /inventory, and /search. Max latency reached 1570 ms, average latency was 418.86 ms. Resource pressure was moderate (max CPU 69.31%, max memory 77.76%, max DB pool 69.13%). Traffic spans multiple dependencies including redis, postgres, identity_provider, and payment_gateway, with mixed deployment versions present.","ai_summary":"catalog-api is experiencing a latency regression rather than a hard outage. The issue is distributed across two hosts and multiple endpoints, with the worst latency on /products and /inventory. Resource and DB pool usage are elevated but not saturated, so this looks like a performance degradation likely tied to request-path or dependency slowdown.","llm_provider":"codex","mcp_evidence_summary":"MCP client call: MCP evidence for catalog-api: 50 events; errors=latency_regression; hosts=catalog-01, catalog-02; endpoints=/inventory, /products, /search; dependencies=identity_provider, none, payment_gateway, postgres; avg_latency_ms=419; max_latency_ms=1570; max_cpu_pct=69; max_db_pool_pct=69.","alert_name":"AIOps - Incident Candidate Alert","host":"unknown-host","mcp_investigation":true,"mcp_tools_used":["splunk_run_query"],"spl_queries_used":[],"mcp_log_event_count":50,"llm_raw_response":"{\n  \"root_cause\": \"Service latency regression in catalog-api\",\n  \"severity\": \"MEDIUM\",\n  \"confidence_score\": 0.85,\n  \"evidence_summary\": \"50 events for catalog-api show sustained latency regression across catalog-01 and catalog-02. Affected endpoints include /products, /inventory, and /search. Max latency reached 1570 ms, average latency was 418.86 ms. Resource pressure was moderate (max CPU 69.31%, max memory 77.76%, max DB pool 69.13%). Traffic spans multiple dependencies including redis, postgres, identity_provider, and payment_gateway, with mixed deployment versions present.\",\n  \"ai_summary\": \"catalog-api is experiencing a latency regression rather than a hard outage. The issue is distributed across two hosts and multiple endpoints, with the worst latency on /products and /inventory. Resource and DB pool usage are elevated but not saturated, so this looks like a performance degradation likely tied to request-path or dependency slowdown.\",\n  \"recommended_actions\": [\n    \"Scale catalog-api instances if latency remains elevated under current load\",\n    \"Inspect slow endpoint paths, especially /products and /inventory\",\n    \"Check dependency latency and connection behavior for postgres, redis, identity_provider, and payment_gateway\",\n    \"Compare performance across deployment versions 2026.06.1, 2026.06.2, and 2026.06.3\"\n  ],\n  \"safe_remediation_actions\": [\n    \"SIMULATE: Scale service instances\",\n    \"SIMULATE: Warm cache\",\n    \"SIMULATE: Inspect slow endpoint\",\n    \"SIMULATE: Review dependency latency and pool usage\"\n  ]\n}\nCodex MCP enhancement failed: [WinError 206] The filename or extension is too long","incident_status":"COMPLETED","investigation_status":"COMPLETED","action":"splunk_webhook_triaged","sourcetype":"aiops-incidents"}
