{"timestamp":"2026-06-14T08:39:31.999+05:30","incident_id":"inc-9cb17b34e3","service":"payment-api","status":"COMPLETED","severity":"HIGH","root_cause":"Upstream dependency failure affecting payment-api requests, likely centered on payment_gateway and identity_provider interactions.","confidence_score":0.85,"evidence_summary":"50 evidence events for payment-api show repeated upstream_api_failure and latency_regression across payment-01 and payment-02. Affected endpoints are /payments/authorize and /payments/capture. Latency spiked to 1650 ms with average 545 ms while CPU stayed moderate at 68% and DB pool at 69%, making resource exhaustion less likely. Failures span multiple regions and deployments, with 502/503 responses present in raw events.","ai_summary":"RCA points to upstream dependency instability rather than an internal capacity issue. The pattern is consistent with external or shared dependency degradation causing elevated latency and intermittent request failures on payment-api.","llm_provider":"codex","mcp_evidence_summary":"MCP client call: MCP evidence for payment-api: 50 events; errors=latency_regression, upstream_api_failure; hosts=payment-01, payment-02; endpoints=/payments/authorize, /payments/capture; dependencies=identity_provider, none, payment_gateway, postgres; avg_latency_ms=545; max_latency_ms=1650; max_cpu_pct=68; max_db_pool_pct=69.","alert_name":"AIOps - Incident Candidate Alert","host":"unknown-host","mcp_investigation":true,"mcp_tools_used":["splunk_run_query"],"spl_queries_used":[],"mcp_log_event_count":50,"llm_raw_response":"{\n  \"root_cause\": \"Upstream dependency failure affecting payment-api requests, likely centered on payment_gateway and identity_provider interactions.\",\n  \"severity\": \"HIGH\",\n  \"confidence_score\": 0.85,\n  \"evidence_summary\": \"50 evidence events for payment-api show repeated upstream_api_failure and latency_regression across payment-01 and payment-02. Affected endpoints are /payments/authorize and /payments/capture. Latency spiked to 1650 ms with average 545 ms while CPU stayed moderate at 68% and DB pool at 69%, making resource exhaustion less likely. Failures span multiple regions and deployments, with 502/503 responses present in raw events.\",\n  \"ai_summary\": \"RCA points to upstream dependency instability rather than an internal capacity issue. The pattern is consistent with external or shared dependency degradation causing elevated latency and intermittent request failures on payment-api.\",\n  \"recommended_actions\": [\n    \"Fail over or reroute traffic away from the failing upstream dependency\",\n    \"Open escalation with the upstream provider or owning team\",\n    \"Throttle or cap retries to prevent amplified load during dependency degradation\",\n    \"Monitor payment-api error rate, p95 latency, and dependency call success rate until stable\"\n  ],\n  \"safe_remediation_actions\": [\n    \"SIMULATE: Fail over upstream dependency\",\n    \"SIMULATE: Open provider escalation\",\n    \"SIMULATE: Throttle retries\"\n  ]\n}\nCodex MCP enhancement failed: [WinError 206] The filename or extension is too long","incident_status":"COMPLETED","investigation_status":"COMPLETED","action":"splunk_webhook_triaged","sourcetype":"aiops-incidents"}
