{"timestamp":"2026-06-14T08:49:34.318+05:30","incident_id":"inc-ee730e04ac","service":"catalog-api","status":"COMPLETED","severity":"CRITICAL","root_cause":"Postgres-backed request latency/timeouts are the most likely cause, with elevated database pool pressure contributing to service-wide latency regression on catalog-api.","confidence_score":0.84,"evidence_summary":"50 evidence events for catalog-api show repeated latency_regression and database_timeout signals across /inventory, /products, and /search on catalog-01 and catalog-02. Latency reached 1958 ms, average latency was 380.68 ms, and DB pool utilization peaked at 69.91% while CPU stayed moderate at 71.85% and memory at 77.53%. The pattern points to database dependency slowness rather than host CPU or memory exhaustion.","ai_summary":"catalog-api is experiencing a database-dependent latency incident. The strongest signal is repeated timeout/latency regression on postgres-backed endpoints with moderate host resource usage and elevated DB pool pressure. This is consistent with a DB bottleneck, connection contention, or downstream query slowness rather than a compute saturation event.","llm_provider":"codex","mcp_evidence_summary":"MCP client call: MCP evidence for catalog-api: 50 events; errors=database_timeout, latency_regression; hosts=catalog-01, catalog-02; endpoints=/inventory, /products, /search; dependencies=identity_provider, none, payment_gateway, postgres; avg_latency_ms=381; max_latency_ms=1958; max_cpu_pct=72; max_db_pool_pct=70.","alert_name":"AIOps - Incident Candidate Alert","host":"unknown-host","mcp_investigation":true,"mcp_tools_used":["splunk_run_query"],"spl_queries_used":[],"mcp_log_event_count":50,"llm_raw_response":"{\n  \"root_cause\": \"Postgres-backed request latency/timeouts are the most likely cause, with elevated database pool pressure contributing to service-wide latency regression on catalog-api.\",\n  \"severity\": \"CRITICAL\",\n  \"confidence_score\": 0.84,\n  \"evidence_summary\": \"50 evidence events for catalog-api show repeated latency_regression and database_timeout signals across /inventory, /products, and /search on catalog-01 and catalog-02. Latency reached 1958 ms, average latency was 380.68 ms, and DB pool utilization peaked at 69.91% while CPU stayed moderate at 71.85% and memory at 77.53%. The pattern points to database dependency slowness rather than host CPU or memory exhaustion.\",\n  \"ai_summary\": \"catalog-api is experiencing a database-dependent latency incident. The strongest signal is repeated timeout/latency regression on postgres-backed endpoints with moderate host resource usage and elevated DB pool pressure. This is consistent with a DB bottleneck, connection contention, or downstream query slowness rather than a compute saturation event.\",\n  \"recommended_actions\": [\n    \"Inspect Postgres query latency, locks, slow queries, and connection usage for catalog-api traffic.\",\n    \"Check application connection pool settings and recycle stuck or idle-in-transaction connections if present.\",\n    \"Scale database capacity or read replicas if sustained query latency is confirmed.\",\n    \"Verify whether recent deploy version 2026.06.3 correlates with the regression on affected endpoints.\"\n  ],\n  \"safe_remediation_actions\": [\n    \"SIMULATE: recycle application DB connections and observe latency and error rate\",\n    \"SIMULATE: temporarily raise connection pool limits within safe bounds and watch DB saturation\",\n    \"SIMULATE: route read-heavy traffic away from Postgres if a replica is available\",\n    \"SIMULATE: roll back or canary the latest catalog-api deployment if regression aligns with version change\"\n  ]\n}\nCodex MCP enhancement failed: [WinError 206] The filename or extens","incident_status":"COMPLETED","investigation_status":"COMPLETED","action":"splunk_webhook_triaged","sourcetype":"aiops-incidents"}
