{"timestamp":"2026-06-14T08:49:54.325+05:30","incident_id":"inc-bc22726cc7","service":"auth-api","status":"COMPLETED","severity":"MEDIUM","root_cause":"Authentication provider instability or token validation failure affecting auth-api requests, most visible on /login and /token/refresh.","confidence_score":0.78,"evidence_summary":"50 events for auth-api across auth-01 and auth-02 show repeated auth_failure plus one latency_regression. Impact spans /login, /session, and /token/refresh with dependencies repeatedly pointing to identity_provider. Latency peaked at 1153 ms while CPU (70.38%), memory (77.78%), and DB pool (69.64%) stayed below clear saturation, making resource exhaustion less likely.","ai_summary":"Most likely failure mode is identity provider or token validation degradation rather than host capacity. Errors cluster around authentication flows, across multiple regions and both hosts, with no strong signal of CPU, memory, or DB pool saturation. The pattern fits intermittent auth backend/provider issues causing retries, failed token refreshes, and latency inflation.","llm_provider":"codex","mcp_evidence_summary":"MCP client call: MCP evidence for auth-api: 50 events; errors=auth_failure, latency_regression; hosts=auth-01, auth-02; endpoints=/login, /session, /token/refresh; dependencies=identity_provider, none, payment_gateway, postgres; avg_latency_ms=302; max_latency_ms=1153; max_cpu_pct=70; max_db_pool_pct=70.","alert_name":"AIOps - Incident Candidate Alert","host":"unknown-host","mcp_investigation":true,"mcp_tools_used":["splunk_run_query"],"spl_queries_used":[],"mcp_log_event_count":50,"llm_raw_response":"{\"root_cause\":\"Authentication provider instability or token validation failure affecting auth-api requests, most visible on /login and /token/refresh.\",\"severity\":\"MEDIUM\",\"confidence_score\":0.78,\"evidence_summary\":\"50 events for auth-api across auth-01 and auth-02 show repeated auth_failure plus one latency_regression. Impact spans /login, /session, and /token/refresh with dependencies repeatedly pointing to identity_provider. Latency peaked at 1153 ms while CPU (70.38%), memory (77.78%), and DB pool (69.64%) stayed below clear saturation, making resource exhaustion less likely.\",\"ai_summary\":\"Most likely failure mode is identity provider or token validation degradation rather than host capacity. Errors cluster around authentication flows, across multiple regions and both hosts, with no strong signal of CPU, memory, or DB pool saturation. The pattern fits intermittent auth backend/provider issues causing retries, failed token refreshes, and latency inflation.\",\"recommended_actions\":[\"Verify identity provider health and recent config or certificate changes\",\"Check token signing/validation keys, issuer/audience settings, and clock skew\",\"Review auth-api error logs and upstream dependency timeouts for /login and /token/refresh\",\"If provider degradation is confirmed, fail over to a healthy identity provider or rollback the last auth-related change\"],\"safe_remediation_actions\":[\"SIMULATE: Validate identity provider failover path\",\"SIMULATE: Revoke/refresh suspect sessions in a non-production environment\",\"SIMULATE: Roll back recent auth or token-validation config changes\",\"SIMULATE: Escalate to the auth service and identity provider owners\"]}\nCodex MCP enhancement failed: [WinError 206] The filename or extension is too long","incident_status":"COMPLETED","investigation_status":"COMPLETED","action":"splunk_webhook_triaged","sourcetype":"aiops-incidents"}
