1534. Resource pressure is present but not critical (max_cpu_pct=72, max_memory_pct=76, max_db_pool_pct=69).\",\n  \"ai_summary\": \"Fallback RCA for auth-api indicates authentication provider or token validation failure. The pattern is supported by repeated auth_failure events on session and token refresh flows, across both hosts, with moderate latency regression and no clear saturation of CPU, memory, or DB pool capacity.\",\n  \"recommended_actions\": [\n    \"Fail over or validate the identity provider path\",\n    \"Inspect token validation, signing keys, and session auth configuration\",\n    \"Invalidate affected sessions and force re-authentication if needed\",\n    \"Escalate to the auth service and identity provider owners\"\n  ],\n  \"safe_remediation_actions\": [\n    \"SIMULATE: Fail over identity provider\",\n    \"SIMULATE: Invalidate bad sessions\",\n    \"SIMULATE: Escalate auth service\"\n  ]\n}\nCodex MCP enhancement failed: [WinError 206] The filename or extension is too long","incident_status":"COMPLETED","investigation_status":"COMPLETED","action":"splunk_webhook_triaged","sourcetype":"aiops-incidents"}
