{"timestamp":"2026-06-14T11:59:28.068+05:30","incident_id":"inc-c40428f43f","service":"auth-api","status":"COMPLETED","severity":"MEDIUM","root_cause":"Primary failure appears to be authentication provider or token validation issues affecting auth-api requests, concentrated on /login and /token/refresh. Latency increased alongside auth failures, but host/resource metrics do not indicate an infrastructure saturation event.","confidence_score":0.85,"evidence_summary":"50 evidence events for auth-api across auth-01 and auth-02. Dominant error type is auth_failure with some latency_regression. Affected endpoints are /login, /session, and /token/refresh. Max latency reached 1509 ms, while max CPU stayed around 72% and max DB pool usage around 70%, which does not strongly support resource exhaustion.","ai_summary":"auth-api incident is most consistent with an authentication provider or token validation problem. Evidence shows repeated auth_failure events on login and token refresh paths, with elevated latency but only moderate CPU and DB pool usage, so the likely issue is dependency/auth flow failure rather than host overload.","mcp_evidence_summary":"MCP client call: MCP evidence for auth-api: 50 events; errors=auth_failure, latency_regression; hosts=auth-01, auth-02; endpoints=/login, /session, /token/refresh; dependencies=identity_provider, none, payment_gateway, postgres; avg_latency_ms=373; max_latency_ms=1509; max_cpu_pct=72; max_db_pool_pct=70.","llm_provider":"codex","mcp_investigation":true,"mcp_tools_used":["splunk_run_query"],"spl_queries_used":[],"mcp_log_event_count":50,"approved_by":null,"remediation_status":"INVESTIGATED","remediation_result":null,"alert_name":"AIOps - Incident Candidate Alert","host":"unknown-host","llm_raw_response":"{\"root_cause\":\"Primary failure appears to be authentication provider or token validation issues affecting auth-api requests, concentrated on /login and /token/refresh. Latency increased alongside auth failures, but host/resource metrics do not indicate an infrastructure saturation event.\",\"severity\":\"MEDIUM\",\"confidence_score\":0.85,\"evidence_summary\":\"50 evidence events for auth-api across auth-01 and auth-02. Dominant error type is auth_failure with some latency_regression. Affected endpoints are /login, /session, and /token/refresh. Max latency reached 1509 ms, while max CPU stayed around 72% and max DB pool usage around 70%, which does not strongly support resource exhaustion.\",\"ai_summary\":\"auth-api incident is most consistent with an authentication provider or token validation problem. Evidence shows repeated auth_failure events on login and token refresh paths, with elevated latency but only moderate CPU and DB pool usage, so the likely issue is dependency/auth flow failure rather than host overload.\",\"recommended_actions\":[\"Validate identity provider availability, response codes, and token signing/validation status\",\"Check for recent config, certificate, key rotation, or audience/issuer changes impacting token verification\",\"Inspect failed /login and /token/refresh traces for common error codes and dependency timeouts\",\"Temporarily fail over to a healthy identity provider path if available\",\"Review session invalidation and refresh-token handling for stale or corrupted tokens\"],\"safe_remediation_actions\":[\"SIMULATE: Fail over identity provider\",\"SIMULATE: Invalidate bad sessions\",\"SIMULATE: Escalate auth service\"]}\nCodex MCP enhancement failed: [WinError 206] The filename or extension is too long","incident_status":"COMPLETED","investigation_status":"COMPLETED","action":"splunk_webhook_triaged","sourcetype":"aiops-incidents"}
