{"timestamp":"2026-06-14T12:09:38.158+05:30","incident_id":"inc-1286d673ad","service":"payment-api","status":"COMPLETED","severity":"HIGH","root_cause":"Upstream dependency failure, most likely affecting payment_gateway and/or identity_provider, causing elevated latency and 503 errors in payment-api.","confidence_score":0.82,"evidence_summary":"50 events for payment-api across payment-01 and payment-02. Repeated upstream_api_failure and latency_regression signals. Affected endpoints were /payments/authorize and /payments/capture. Max latency reached 1472 ms, average latency was 496.3 ms. Resource pressure was moderate, with max CPU 71.59% and max DB pool 68.27%, which is less consistent with an internal saturation issue than with dependency-induced slowdown.","ai_summary":"Incident is consistent with an upstream dependency failure rather than a primary service overload. Payment-api is showing repeated latency regressions and 503s on authorize/capture paths while CPU and DB pool usage remain below critical levels. The most plausible trigger is intermittent failure or slow response from payment_gateway and related dependency paths.","mcp_evidence_summary":"MCP client call: MCP evidence for payment-api: 50 events; errors=latency_regression, upstream_api_failure; hosts=payment-01, payment-02; endpoints=/payments/authorize, /payments/capture; dependencies=identity_provider, none, payment_gateway, postgres; avg_latency_ms=496; max_latency_ms=1472; max_cpu_pct=72; max_db_pool_pct=68.","llm_provider":"codex","mcp_investigation":true,"mcp_tools_used":["splunk_run_query"],"spl_queries_used":[],"mcp_log_event_count":50,"approved_by":null,"remediation_status":"INVESTIGATED","remediation_result":null,"alert_name":"AIOps - Incident Candidate Alert","host":"unknown-host","llm_raw_response":"{\n  \"root_cause\": \"Upstream dependency failure, most likely affecting payment_gateway and/or identity_provider, causing elevated latency and 503 errors in payment-api.\",\n  \"severity\": \