{"timestamp":"2026-06-14T14:37:47.514+05:30","incident_id":"inc-20260614090622-2d10bb","service":"checkout-api","status":"COMPLETED","severity":"CRITICAL","root_cause":"Database connection pool saturation in checkout-api's postgres dependency, manifesting as database_timeout errors on /checkout and driving elevated latency and 5xx responses.","confidence_score":0.95,"evidence_summary":"Splunk confirmed 17 incident events for checkout-api with a single error type, database_timeout, all on endpoint /checkout and dependent on postgres. Aggregate incident stats show avg latency 2710.41 ms, max latency 4084 ms, avg DB pool utilization 95.76%, max DB pool utilization 98.87%, avg CPU 62.33%, and max CPU 81.75%. Raw events came from checkout-01, checkout-02, and checkout-03 and included 500/502/503/504 responses across deployment versions 2026.06.1, 2026.06.2, and 2026.06.3. The data supports a database-side saturation/timeout failure rather than a primary CPU or memory outage.","ai_summary":"Evidence points to checkout-api being bottlenecked on postgres connection availability. The incident is concentrated on /checkout, with all sampled events showing database_timeout and near-max DB pool usage, while CPU and memory are elevated but secondary.","mcp_evidence_summary":"MCP client call: MCP evidence for checkout-api: 17 events; errors=database_timeout; hosts=checkout-01, checkout-02, checkout-03; endpoints=/checkout; dependencies=postgres; avg_latency_ms=2710; max_latency_ms=4084; max_cpu_pct=82; max_db_pool_pct=99.","llm_provider":"codex_mcp_agent","mcp_investigation":true,"mcp_tools_used":["splunk_run_query"],"spl_queries_used":["index=main sourcetype=agentic-ops (incident_id=\"inc-20260614090622-2d10bb\" OR service=\"checkout-api\") | stats count as event_count avg(latency_ms) as avg_latency_ms max(latency_ms) as max_latency_ms max(cpu_pct) as max_cpu_pct max(db_connection_pool_pct) as max_db_pool_pct by service host endpoint error_type","index=main sourcetype=agentic-ops