{"timestamp":"2026-06-14T14:47:05.199+05:30","incident_id":"inc-b66570ce98","service":"auth-api","status":"COMPLETED","severity":"MEDIUM","root_cause":"Authentication provider or token validation failure affecting auth-api","confidence_score":0.85,"evidence_summary":"50 evidence events for auth-api. auth_failure is the dominant error with some latency_regression. Impact spans auth-01 and auth-02 across /login, /session, and /token/refresh. Identity_provider is the primary dependency seen during failures. Latency peaked at 4111 ms with avg 667 ms, while CPU (71.9%), memory (80.8%), and DB pool (69.31%) were elevated but not saturated. Mixed deployment versions (2026.06.1-2026.06.3) suggest the issue is unlikely to be pure capacity exhaustion.","ai_summary":"The incident is most consistent with authentication validation or upstream identity provider instability rather than a broad infrastructure outage. Errors are concentrated on auth flows and token refresh paths, with moderate resource pressure and cross-region occurrence. This supports a service-level auth dependency issue as the primary cause.","mcp_evidence_summary":"MCP client call: MCP evidence for auth-api: 50 events; errors=auth_failure, latency_regression; hosts=auth-01, auth-02; endpoints=/login, /session, /token/refresh; dependencies=identity_provider, none, payment_gateway, postgres; avg_latency_ms=667; max_latency_ms=4111; max_cpu_pct=72; max_db_pool_pct=69.","llm_provider":"codex","mcp_investigation":true,"mcp_tools_used":["splunk_run_query"],"spl_queries_used":[],"mcp_log_event_count":50,"approved_by":null,"remediation_status":"INVESTIGATED","remediation_result":null,"alert_name":"AIOps - Incident Candidate Alert","host":"unknown-host","llm_raw_response":"{\n  \"root_cause\": \"Authentication provider or token validation failure affecting auth-api\",\n  \"severity\": \"MEDIUM\",\n  \"confidence_score\": 0.85,\n  \"evidence_summary\": \"50 evidence events for auth-api. auth_failure is the dominant error with some latency_regression. Impact spans auth-01 and auth-02 across /login, /session, and /token/refresh. Identity_provider is the primary dependency seen during failures. Latency peaked at 4111 ms with avg 667 ms, while CPU (71.9%), memory (80.8%), and DB pool (69.31%) were elevated but not saturated. Mixed deployment versions (2026.06.1-2026.06.3) suggest the issue is unlikely to be pure capacity exhaustion.\",\n  \"ai_summary\": \"The incident is most consistent with authentication validation or upstream identity provider instability rather than a broad infrastructure outage. Errors are concentrated on auth flows and token refresh paths, with moderate resource pressure and cross-region occurrence. This supports a service-level auth dependency issue as the primary cause.\",\n  \"recommended_actions\": [\n    \"Fail over or quarantine the identity provider path\",\n    \"Invalidate impacted sessions and force re-authentication for affected users\",\n    \"Escalate to auth service owners to inspect token validation, auth backend health, and recent deployment differences\"\n  ],\n  \"safe_remediation_actions\": [\n    \"SIMULATE: Fail over identity provider\",\n    \"SIMULATE: Invalidate impacted sessions\",\n    \"SIMULATE: Escalate auth service investigation\"\n  ]\n}\nCodex MCP enhancement failed: [WinError 206] The filename or extension is too long","incident_status":"COMPLETED","investigation_status":"COMPLETED","action":"splunk_webhook_triaged","sourcetype":"aiops-incidents"}
